Sonia&rsquo;s mind drifted to thoughts of Henry, imagining him holding the key, deciding when and if she would ever be released. The idea of being used by him, of surrendering to his will, sent shivers down her spine. The anticipation of what lay ahead filled her with a strange mix of anxiety and arousal.
As the night wore on, Sonia began to process her new reality. The chastity belt wasn&rsquo;t just a physical barrier; it was a symbol of her trust in Henry and her commitment to this path. It forced her to confront her desires, her boundaries, and the depths of her submission.
Despite the discomfort and the lingering unease, Sonia found a sense of peace in her decision. She had chosen this life, this role, and she was determined to embrace it fully. As she finally drifted into a fitful sleep, the belt remained a constant unyielding reminder of what she now was.
His.

The Green Gala opens# The day of the Green Gala was busy as Mara worked with Fleur and her staff to ensure everything was perfect. Once the final touches were done, it was time for Mara to get ready.
Philippe had arranged a hotel suite for Mara to change, and Liliane, a skilled dresser and makeup artist, was there to help. Mara smiled behind her mask, noticing the floral-themed names of the staff. Increasingly, shops and venues were putting their women into uniforms, and the hotel was apparently taking this one step further, making the name plates part of the uniform scheme as well.
Liliane started with Mara’s hair and makeup, enhancing her natural beauty while keeping it simple under the circumstances. Philippe made sure her outfit was ready. Mara undressed down to her iGuardian and then slipped into the base layer: ballet boots and a latex suit that hugged her form.
The main part of the outfit came next. Liliane and Philippe helped her into a stiff hobble skirt designed to look like the bark of an ancient tree. The skirt was so tight it kept Mara’s legs close together, forcing her to take tiny steps. The dress continued upward, covering her torso and face in bark-like material. Her face was entirely hidden, except for a small, concealed feed port a and tiny eye holes. The headdress was a large, green crown that resembled the leafy top of a tree.
Her arms were also covered in the bark-like material, which gave them the look of moss-covered tree branches. Though her movements were slow and restricted, she could still use her arms to sign, even if gripping things was impossible.
When Mara looked in the mirror, she saw a figure that resembled an ancient moving tree. The stiffness of the dress and the bark-like covering made it clear she wouldn&rsquo;t be able to sit or move quickly. She felt a strange mix of vulnerability and security, knowing she was silent and slow, yet still able to communicate with her hands.
Philippe noticed her taking in her reflection. &ldquo;Are you comfortable, Mara?&rdquo; he asked gently.
&ldquo;Yes, Sir. It’s different, but I’ll manage,&rdquo; she signed.
Philippe smiled and placed a reassuring hand on her shoulder. &ldquo;You look stunning. I know it’s a demanding dress. Keep in mind that I’m here to help you through the evening.&rdquo;
Mara took a small step, feeling the stiffness of the dress and the restriction in her movement. &ldquo;Thank you, Sir. I appreciate your support.&rdquo;
As they prepared to leave the suite, Philippe guided her with a firm yet caring touch, making sure she felt secure despite her limited movement. The tight hobble skirt, heavy headdress, and stiff covering made every movement slow and steady. But within the restrictions, there was a comfort in knowing Philippe was there to guide her.
&ldquo;Let&rsquo;s make this an evening to remember,&rdquo; Philippe said as he led Mara to the lift that would take them down to the entrance.
As guests began to arrive, Mara and Philippe stood at the entrance of the grand ballroom, ready to greet them. The guests showcased the unique blend of elegance and restriction that defined Changed society.
Some guests arrived in ballgowns with floral Victorian skirts or hair adorned with green vines, embodying the theme of Nature&rsquo;s Elegance. They curtsied politely to Mara and Philippe, exchanging formal pleasantries.
Lord Hargreaves&rsquo; Caroline emerged from the limousine, the back of her dress rising and engulfing her in a protective shell.
Then came Lord Hargreaves, the well-known British philanthropist. He helped his ward, Caroline, out of the limousine. She emerged in a complicated white dress reminiscent of lotus petals, scandalously leaving her shoulders, head, face, and hair uncovered.
But Mara barely caught a glimpse of Caroline’s slender body and platinum blonde hair because the back of her dress came to life. It rose above her head, grabbed her, and engulfed her, forming a pearlescent protective shell around her, leaving only a small slit for her to see through. Lord Hargreaves guided her with a gentle yet firm hand.
Caroline&rsquo;s dress clammed shut, engulfing her in a protective shell, leaving only a small slit for her to see through.
&ldquo;Good evening, Lord Hargreaves,&rdquo; Philippe greeted respectfully. &ldquo;Caroline, your outfit is exquisite.&rdquo;
&ldquo;Thank you, Philippe,&rdquo; Lord Hargreaves replied proudly. &ldquo;Bioengineering is making fantastic progress these days. It helps us stay alive and creates art and fashion.&rdquo;
Mara was impressed by Caroline&rsquo;s living, breathing piece of art. “You look beautiful, Caroline.”
Caroline&rsquo;s enclosed form curtsied, and Mara heard a faint murmur from the shell, &ldquo;Thank you, Madam Mara.&rdquo;
The next limousine arrived, and Henry and Sonia emerged. Philippe smiled warmly at their elegant ensembles. Sonia&rsquo;s dress was a stunning blend of latex and silk in varying shades of green, adorned with real bamboo pieces. The bodice was a high-necked corset with intricate patterns mimicking bamboo stalks, tightly laced to enforce an impeccable posture. The skirt, layered with latex leaves, created the illusion of a flowing bamboo forest, but it narrowed towards the hem, forming a restrictive hobble skirt.
Sonia&rsquo;s sleeves were long and fitted, ending in delicate mittens connected to the dress with thin, decorative chains, ensuring her hands remained at her sides. A high, stiff collar framed her neck, leading to a beautifully crafted mask shaped like bamboo leaves, decorated with small, sparkling emeralds. The mask covered her face but left her mouth free. Her hair was styled into an elegant updo, adorned with bamboo-shaped hairpins.
Henry wore a classical suit in shades of green and gold to complement Sonia&rsquo;s dress. His suit was tailored to perfection, exuding elegance and authority. Henry helped Sonia out of the car and guided her with a gentle but firm hand on her back.
&ldquo;Good evening, Henry,&rdquo; Philippe greeted warmly. &ldquo;Sonia, you look absolutely enchanting.&rdquo;
Sonia, feeling both restricted and supported, curtsied with Henry&rsquo;s assistance. &ldquo;Good evening, Sir. Thank you for your kind words. The theme of nature&rsquo;s elegance truly inspired us.&rdquo;
Mara admired Sonia’s dress. “Your outfit is a masterpiece, Sonia. The bamboo elements are striking.”
&ldquo;Thank you, Mara,&rdquo; Sonia replied gently. &ldquo;We wanted to embrace the theme as fully as possible.&rdquo;
Henry nodded in agreement, his eyes twinkling with pride. &ldquo;Maylee Shufoo outdid themselves with the &lsquo;Enchanted Bamboo&rsquo;. It’s both beautiful and symbolic of our commitment to sustainability.&rdquo;
Philippe nodded appreciatively. &ldquo;Indeed. The craftsmanship is remarkable. I&rsquo;m pleased to see such dedication to the theme.&rdquo;
As Henry guided Sonia further into the ballroom, William Lemieux and his ward, Helena, arrived. Helena was encased in a thick black latex catsuit that covered her from head to toe, with matching eye covers. The only visible openings were the breathing holes in her nose and a cleverly hidden feed port under her left ear. Over the latex, she wore a wide skirt made from layers of transparent white gauze and a flowing harem blouse, revealing the shiny latex beneath.
&ldquo;Sir William,&rdquo; Philippe greeted warmly. &ldquo;Your ward&rsquo;s ensemble is truly remarkable.&rdquo;
&ldquo;Thank you, Philippe,&rdquo; William replied proudly. &ldquo;Helena put a lot of effort into this.&rdquo;
Mara looked at Helena, her voice gentle. &ldquo;Helena, you look stunning. The combination of textures is beautiful.&rdquo;
Helena nodded, the faint outline of her smile visible through the latex. She quickly looked to William, and when he nodded assent, she signed. &ldquo;Thank you, Mara. You look enchanting as well.&rdquo;
The excitement grew as celebrity guests arrived. Photographers and reporters buzzed with anticipation, their cameras ready. Harry Styles was the first to emerge from an electric limo.
Harry&rsquo;s outfit caught everyone&rsquo;s attention. He wore a formal Victorian tailcoat made entirely of living green leaves. Reporters flocked to him, curious and admiring.
&ldquo;Harry, can you tell us about your outfit?&rdquo; one reporter asked.
Harry smiled, turning slightly for the cameras. &ldquo;This dress is a creation of BioGreen Innovations,&rdquo; he explained. &ldquo;It was grown on me using the latest British biotech. The leaves are alive and will keep growing throughout the evening. It&rsquo;s all about celebrating nature and sustainability.&rdquo;
The name BioGreen Innovations quickly became a buzzword among the reporters, who marveled at the living, breathing masterpiece. The dress showcased cutting-edge technology perfectly aligned with the Green Gala theme.
The crowd&rsquo;s attention shifted as a loud whirring announced Zendaya&rsquo;s arrival in an electric hexacopter drone. She stepped out, drawing gasps from the crowd.
Zendaya stepped in front of the crowd with her head and face uncovered.
Zendaya wore a metallic red full-body suit that highlighted her curves. Flowers and leaves sprouted from the suit&rsquo;s joints, symbolizing nature reclaiming its place. A crown of thorns and flowers sat on her head, barely covering her hair. Her outfit represented the blend of technology and nature.
Reporters quickly noticed the most shocking detail. &ldquo;Zendaya, you’re not wearing a mask or head covering. This is unprecedented!&rdquo;
Her bare face and uncovered hair stood out against the strict norms of Changed society. She smiled confidently. &ldquo;Tonight is about celebrating harmony between nature and technology. My outfit represents the decay of old technologies and the resurgence of nature. It&rsquo;s about balance.&rdquo;
Mara watched from beside Philippe, feeling worried about Zendaya&rsquo;s bold move. &ldquo;Her outfit is fantastic, but Zendaya&rsquo;s face-immodesty has me deeply worried. Quick, what can we do?&rdquo; Bound and restricted, Mara couldn&rsquo;t intervene.
Disapproval spread through the crowd. Reporters and traditional guests were taken aback by Zendaya&rsquo;s appearance. Whispers of scandal filled the air, and photographers captured the growing discontent.
Event staff acting as an informal &ldquo;fashion police,&rdquo; approached Zendaya, veils and masks in hand. Before they reached her, Tom Holland emerged from the hexacopter, looking concerned. &ldquo;Zendaya, wait!&rdquo; he called, hurrying after her with the missing piece of her outfit—a robot head.
The staff paused, allowing Tom to catch up. &ldquo;I told you to wait and dress properly. This is unacceptable,&rdquo; he said quietly but sternly.
He retrieved the headpiece and, with the help of the staff, carefully locked it into place. The headpiece completed her outfit, rendering her modestly covered, gagged, and unable to speak.
&ldquo;Zendaya, you know the expectations,&rdquo; Tom scolded. &ldquo;You will always be dressed properly, especially at such a high-profile event.&rdquo;
Mara observed as Zendaya hand-danced her apologies, her fingers moving with contrition. &ldquo;I apologize, Sir,&rdquo; Zendaya&rsquo;s hands conveyed. &ldquo;I thought the theme would allow for more freedom. I didn&rsquo;t mean to cause trouble.&rdquo;
Tom&rsquo;s eyes softened slightly, but he remained firm. &ldquo;You will always be appropriately covered. Now, let’s proceed with the evening as planned.&rdquo;
With her head now covered, Zendaya was silenced and her presence became less of a focal point. Tom&rsquo;s decisive action calmed the audience, who began to relax and refocus on the evening&rsquo;s festivities.
Throughout the evening, Tom stayed close to Zendaya, ensuring she adhered to societal expectations. He guided her through the ballroom, managing their interactions with calm authority. Traditional guests nodded approvingly, seeing his actions as a reaffirmation of their values.
Mara watched, sensing an opportunity to control the media narrative. She turned to Philippe. &ldquo;Sir, perhaps we could frame this episode as a bold statement aligned with the theme. It would help manage public perception and highlight the event&rsquo;s focus on harmony between nature and technology. Zendaya&rsquo;s outfit could be increasingly restrictive, …&rdquo;
Philippe nodded thoughtfully. &ldquo;An excellent idea, Mara. Here’s how we will handle it.&rdquo;
He faced her fully, his eyes serious. &ldquo;We will present Zendaya’s initial appearance as a deliberate artistic choice, symbolizing the balance between freedom and restraint, technology and nature. I’ll speak to the press and explain that her outfit was designed to evolve throughout the evening, representing the dynamic relationship between our natural world and the technologies we create.&rdquo;
Philippe continued, calm and authoritative. &ldquo;I will highlight the thematic relevance, emphasizing that the transformation of her outfit was part of the evening&rsquo;s narrative. We need to restrain ourselves and always keep discipline to live in harmony with nature. This will frame the situation positively, showcasing our event&rsquo;s innovative spirit and commitment to sustainability.&rdquo;
Mara’s eyes sparkled with admiration. “Thank you, Sir. Your approach will help control the narrative. Maybe you want to inform Tom Holland of that approach, and suggest he plays along, restraining Zendaya more as the evening advances?”
Philippe smiled, placing a gentle hand on her shoulder. &ldquo;Excellent suggestion. You have a keen eye for strategy, Mara. Together, we will ensure this evening is remembered for all the right reasons.&rdquo;

Plans involving Art and Fashion# While their wards relaxed on the veranda, Philippe and Henry sat in the living room, enjoying classical music. Dressed in tailored suits, they sipped their drinks and talked about their love for the opera.
&ldquo;It’s been ages since I went to a performance,&rdquo; Henry said, a bit wistfully. &ldquo;Work&rsquo;s been nonstop, but an evening at the opera would be perfect.&rdquo;
Philippe nodded. &ldquo;There’s something timeless about it. The music, the drama, the elegance.&rdquo;
Henry’s eyes lit up. &ldquo;Have you seen Il Seraglio? It’s coming to the Grand Théâtre soon.&rdquo;
Philippe smiled. &ldquo;Il Seraglio is a great choice. The themes of captivity and freedom are powerful, and the setting is so rich and exotic.&rdquo;
Henry leaned forward, excited. &ldquo;It’s also a chance to dress up and enjoy high fashion. How about we dress our wards to match the theme of the opera?&rdquo;
Philippe chuckled. &ldquo;High fashion with a harem theme? That sounds like a fascinating mix of art and discipline. Mara could wear something that captures the essence of Il Seraglio.&rdquo;
Henry nodded, already imagining it. &ldquo;I can see Sonia in an outfit inspired by the seraglio, with plenty of veils and elements that symbolize captivity, yet elegant enough for the opera.&rdquo;
Philippe’s eyes sparkled. &ldquo;For Mara, something rich, maybe silk and brocade, adorned with jewels to show her status.&rdquo;
Henry added, &ldquo;And for Sonia, a gown with layers of sheer fabric, representing the veils of the harem, yet structured to ensure discipline and posture.&rdquo;
Philippe leaned back, picturing the scene. &ldquo;It would be a spectacle to see our wards dressed like that, capturing the essence of the opera. It’s settled then. We’ll attend Il Seraglio together in my box at the Grand Théâtre. There’s room for four, so it’s perfect.&rdquo;
Henry raised his glass. &ldquo;To opera and high fashion. And to the exquisite blend of art, discipline, and elegance that awaits us.&rdquo;
Philippe smiled and clinked his glass with Henry’s. &ldquo;To an unforgettable evening at the opera.&rdquo; As they discussed more details, their excitement grew, knowing this evening would perfectly blend their passions.
Sonia, dressed in her maid outfit, prepared breakfast for Henry. The white apron and gloves contrasted with her dark dress, and a corset tightly cinched her waist. Having served, she knelt down on her cushion beside Henry, assuming her usual pose—hands behind her back, chest forward, and bottom out. The corset and dress enforced her posture as she waited to be fed.
Henry sat down, smiling as he appreciated her submissive stance. &ldquo;Good morning, Sonia,&rdquo; he said, reaching for a piece of fruit. &ldquo;I received an email from Philippe this morning. We’ll be attending the opera next Saturday, Il Seraglio.&rdquo; He paused as Sonia accepted the bite.
Sonia&rsquo;s eyes lit up with excitement. &ldquo;That&rsquo;s wonderful news, Sir,&rdquo; she said, looking up at him. &ldquo;May I ask if you have plans for my attire? The theme seems perfectly aligned with our shared interests.&rdquo;
Henry nodded, feeding her another bite. &ldquo;I do have some ideas, Sonia. You will indeed be dressed to match the theme.&rdquo;
Sonia felt a thrill of anticipation. &ldquo;Sir, if it pleases you, may I inquire about my role during the evening? Will I be more ornamental or active?&rdquo; Her eyes were soft and pleading as she continued. &ldquo;I’ve grown to love the opera, Sir, and would greatly enjoy wearing a dress that allows me to hear and see the performance. I hope this aligns with your plans.&rdquo;
Henry looked down at her, thoughtful. &ldquo;I assure you, Sonia, I’ve considered your enjoyment. You will be ornamental, but I’ve designed something that will let you appreciate the performance fully.&rdquo;
Sonia&rsquo;s eyes sparkled with gratitude. &ldquo;Thank you, Sir. That means the world to me.&rdquo;
Henry smiled, feeding her another bite. &ldquo;You will look exquisite, Sonia. The dress will reflect the opulence and exoticism of Il Seraglio while ensuring you remain appropriately restrained and elegant.&rdquo;
Sonia knew Henry’s plans for her attire would be both challenging and beautiful.
&ldquo;Now,&rdquo; Henry continued, selecting the next bite for Sonia, &ldquo;let’s finish breakfast. We have much to prepare for the coming days.&rdquo;
At Philippe&rsquo;s home, Mara sat secured to her chair at the breakfast table. As usual, Philippe had connected her feed bag to her mask himself, gently delivering her meal. He then sat across from her, calm and composed as he began to speak.
&ldquo;Mara,&rdquo; Philippe said, breaking the silence. &ldquo;I have news. We will be attending the opera next Saturday, in ten days. We’ll meet Henry and Sonia there.&rdquo;
Mara&rsquo;s eyes brightened with excitement, her gloved fingers moving to sign her response. &ldquo;I’m looking forward to that, Sir. It will be wonderful to see Sonia again.&rdquo;
Philippe nodded with a smile. &ldquo;Indeed. The opera will be Il Seraglio.&rdquo;
Mara&rsquo;s excitement grew, her hands dancing with anticipation. Philippe continued, &ldquo;I’m thinking of dressing you as Konstanze, Mara. You’ll be veiled and chained, as befits a captive woman in a seraglio.&rdquo;
Mara’s heart sank slightly at the thought of being dressed in chains and without a mask. She wouldn’t be able to sign and would have to speak, which made her uneasy. She disliked using her voice. But she knew better than to directly express her discomfort.
Her fingers moved slowly, carefully signing, &ldquo;Sir, I understand your wishes, and I will of course fulfill my assigned role. However, if it pleases you, I would feel more comfortable being masked. I find using my voice&hellip; less modest. Hand-dancing is more expressive and feminine, I believe.&rdquo;
Philippe watched her closely, noticing the careful way she made her request. He considered her words, then nodded thoughtfully. &ldquo;I understand, Mara. If it makes you more comfortable, I will reconsider. You will still be chained, but I’ll ensure you can sign, though within limits.&rdquo;
Mara’s eyes softened with relief, and her hands moved gracefully in gratitude. &ldquo;Thank you, Sir, for your thoughtful consideration. I am most grateful.&rdquo;
Philippe’s smile widened, pleased with her response. &ldquo;Good. You will look stunning as my Konstanze, and I’m sure you will perform admirably. Now, let’s finish our breakfast.&rdquo;
Mara folded her hands in her lap, feeling a deep sense of gratitude as she waited for the feed bag to empty while Philippe ate.
Saturday evening arrived with an air of anticipation and elegance. Philippe guided Mara out of the bathroom, where her iGuardian had just completed its cleaning cycle. The cleaning station released her from its locks, leaving her fresh and ready for the evening ahead. On the bed, the rich, dark red silk dress awaited her, each piece laid out, promising both opulence and confinement.
Philippe helped Mara sit on the edge of the bed. He started by gently removing her ballet boots, carefully unlocking the fasteners and sliding them off her feet. Next, he peeled off her stockings. Mara wasn&rsquo;t used to the cool air on her bare skin, but before she could feel uneasy, Philippe began to dress her for the evening.
He retrieved a pair of silk stockings, their material shimmering. Philippe slowly rolled them up her legs, smoothing out any wrinkles and ensuring they fit snugly. Once the stockings were clipped to the garters of the iGuardian, he reached for the high-heeled knee boots, matching the deep red of her dress and adorned with small gold buckles. He laced them up carefully, making sure each tie was secure before locking the buckles in place.
He led Mara to her vanity, locking her in place so she could apply her makeup and fix her hair while he tended to his own attire. Mara powdered her hair lightly, arranging it into a high, elegant updo. She interspersed the powdered locks with delicate flowers and threads of gold, each piece placed to create a look of aristocratic elegance. Then she laid out her final touches: a pearl necklace and matching earrings, and waited for Philippe to return, unlock her, and finish dressing her.
Philippe, dressed in a distinguished midnight blue velvet tailcoat with gold-embroidered lapels and embossed gold buttons, completed his own preparations. Draped diagonally across his chest was a crimson silk sash adorned with miniature medals and honors. His crisp white silk shirt featured a high stiff collar and a deep crimson tie, perfectly complementing the ensemble. Slim-cut trousers with a subtle gold braid on the outer seam and polished black patent leather Oxfords completed the look. A golden brooch of the Royal Coat of Arms and a black opera cloak lined with crimson silk added the final touches of refined elegance.
He then turned his attention back to Mara. He slipped her hands into the red velvet opera gloves, embroidered with intricate gold designs. The gloves reached up to her shoulders, where he fastened them to the braces of the iGuardian, ensuring they stayed in place throughout the evening.
Unlocking her, Philippe then helped Mara to her feet to guide her into her numerous skirts. The lowest layer was her smooth and narrow Yoyah Sheengzoh, tightly encasing her legs and restricting her step. He layered several petticoats over it, adding volume and structure to her silhouette. The richly decorated and heavy skirt followed, its weight settling around her hips as he adjusted the fabric.
Next, Philippe picked up the stiff embroidered bodice. He carefully positioned it on Mara, making sure it aligned perfectly with the skirt before buttoning it up the back. The final button was locked into place, securing the bodice to the skirt and ensuring there would be no shifting or loosening as the evening progressed.
With the main parts of her dress in place, Philippe then reached for the mask. The mask was a work of art, intricately painted with swirling patterns of gold and crimson, designed to match her dress. It featured a demanding gag, crafted to fit her mouth precisely. Philippe carefully positioned it over Mara’s face, then began the process of working the gag into her mouth. He had to shift it back and forth slightly, ensuring it settled correctly, until Mara could bite down on it. Once it was secure, Philippe clicked the mask to her collar, fixing her head in place. A thin chiffon veil was attached to the mask, insubstantial and semi-transparent, more of an elegant afterthought that allowed the beauty of the mask beneath to show through.
Finally, Philippe took a set of heavy manacles and clasped them around Mara’s wrists. The chains between them were long enough to allow her to sign, though they restricted her movements, preventing her from lifting her hands above elbow level. He fastened the chain to a hardpoint on the iGuardian through a small front opening in her dress, ensuring it was secure while still giving her some freedom to communicate.
Mara stood before Philippe, transformed into Konstanze, a vision of restrained elegance and beauty, ready for the opera.

Intermission# When Mara said, &ldquo;Love is shown through the discipline that shapes us into our true selves,&rdquo; Sonia’s thoughts drifted back to her early days with Henry. She remembered how his guidance had helped her become the person she wanted to be. She had given herself to him completely, and he had fully embraced her in return. Sonia smiled under her veil, recalling how the chastity belt no longer stayed locked once they fully embraced their unequal relationship. As Mara had once said, &ldquo;A ward silently enjoys what her guardian offers.&rdquo;
As the chaos subsided, Philippe checked outside. When it seemed safe, they cautiously returned to the foyer where they met with Henry. As quickly as her chained legs allowed, Sonia glided over to him and leaned into his embrace. The only evidence of the disturbance was broken glass, as Directeur Perroux addressed the guests, assuring them that everything was under control and the show would go on.
Mara processed the events, realizing how quickly Philippe and Henry had prioritized their wards&rsquo; safety. She felt a deep sense of gratitude and admiration for Philippe&rsquo;s protective instincts. Glancing at Sonia, who seemed equally affected, their eyes met, sharing a mutual sense of relief and thankfulness for their guardians&rsquo; quick actions.
&ldquo;Are you alright, Sonia?&rdquo; Henry asked gently.
Sonia curtsied and answered, &ldquo;Yes, Sir. Thank you for protecting us.&rdquo;
Philippe reassured Mara, and they all returned to their seats. As the second act began, Mara leaned closer to Philippe, feeling an even deeper connection. She was his ward, and he was her guardian—her anchor in a world of uncertainty.
Meanwhile, on stage, Blondchen began to reject Osmin&rsquo;s rude advances in her aria &ldquo;Durch Zärtlichkeit und Schmeicheln.&rdquo; Mara smiled behind her mask, thinking, &ldquo;If Blondchen only knew…&rdquo;
After the finale, Philippe secured a private VIP box at the Carré d’Or. He ordered red wine and Turkish delight for Henry, Sonia, and himself, while the women, securely locked to their seats, were unchained. As they were being served, Sonia noticed something unusual. The waitress, named-tagged as Janice on her uniform, wore a discreet &ldquo;S&rdquo; pin pinned to her dress. Sonia knew what that meant—Janice was really a man, an abusive guardian serving a year and a day–a Shadow year, hence the S–as a ward to learn proper restraint and gain a new perspective.
Sonia discreetly signed to Mara, asking if she had noticed the pin. Before Mara could respond, Henry caught sight of Sonia’s gossiping. His expression hardened. This was the second time he caught Sonia signing about other wards corrections behind his back. He did not know why she was obsessed with that, but he could certainly oblige once they were back at home.
&ldquo;Sonia,&rdquo; Henry said firmly, in a low but clear voice, &ldquo;stop that. I thought I had made myself clear. Gossiping about corrections is unacceptable. Corrections are private matters, meant to guide and help you grow. Once they’re done, they are not spoken of again, especially not in public. For all practical purposes, Janice is a ward, and she is to subject to exactly the same expectations and standards as any other ward.&rdquo;
Sonia immediately lowered her gaze, her hands moving with full formality as she signed, &ldquo;I apologize, Sir. Thank you for keeping me aligned.&rdquo;
Henry nodded, his expression softening slightly. &ldquo;See that you remember this, Sonia. We will discuss it further at home.&rdquo; Sonia turned her attention to the Turkish delight and the wine, musing the exact nature of the &ldquo;discussion&rdquo; she&rsquo;d be having with Henry at home. Meanwhile, Janice retured with a feed bag for Mara, which Philippe attached to her feed port himself.
The conversation between the men turned to the Freeborn attack, leaving the women to themselves.
&ldquo;It seems too convenient that this attack happened just as the new Swiss banking transparency laws are coming into effect,&rdquo; Philippe remarked. &ldquo;These laws will expose many hidden fortunes in previously anonymous Swiss accounts and vaults, subjecting them to proper wealth taxes. The timing is suspicious.&rdquo;
Henry nodded but offered a different perspective. &ldquo;I see your point, Philippe, but we must consider all possibilities. It&rsquo;s possible that Chinese-sponsored terror groups could be fueling these masked attacks. They have their own reasons for destabilizing the region, especially with their increasing influence in global affairs.&rdquo;
Sonia wisely remained silent. She was cautious, understanding the delicate balance of their roles, and refrained from interrupting her already upset guardian. Besides, her knowledge of the true origin of the LASS-VASH-2024 was secret and maybe not even relevant in their men&rsquo;s discussion.
The men debated various motivations behind the attack, and eventually, it was time to leave. The men re-secured their wards and led them to the waiting limousine.
At home, Mara thanked Philippe for the wonderful evening and the opera experience. &ldquo;Thank you, Sir. It was a wonderful experience,&rdquo; she signed with genuine gratitude.
Philippe smiled, pleased, and helped her prepare for the night, locking her to the bed in her usual attire. Mara felt a sense of peace and safety as Philippe ensured every detail was just right. As she lay down, feeling the familiar constraints of her night setup, she felt happy and protected. With a contented sigh, she closed her eyes and drifted into a deep, restful sleep.

The Conference# The next morning, the group gathered for brunch at Henry’s place. Anna wore a 1950s flower-print dress with large petticoats, a cinched waist, and long sleeves. She had on short blue leather gloves and a matching headscarf, with a mask concealing her face, completing the vintage look. Sonia was dressed in a floor-length gray pencil skirt and a white blouse buttoned at the back. Her elbow-length leather gloves tucked under the cuffs, and she wore a straw hat pinned to her bun. She was masked as well. Mara, in her usual attire, had on a bonnet and a mask fixed to the collar of her iGuardian, keeping her head still. She wore a white blouse locked in the back, an Edwardian walking skirt in deep navy blue, and her usual ballet knee-boots under the Yoyah Sheengzoh.
The women, locked to their chairs, signed to each other while the men talked outside on the terrace, their conversation taking on a more serious tone.
Anna glanced around before signing to Mara. The leather of her tight gloves creaked as she signed, &ldquo;I heard there was an attack during the intermission. What happened?&rdquo;
Mara’s fingers moved gracefully. &ldquo;Yes, a group of &lsquo;Freeborn&rsquo; tried to &lsquo;free&rsquo; us. It was chaotic, but the Grenadiers managed to stop them quickly.&rdquo;
Sonia added, &ldquo;Apparently, a woman noticed the attackers beforehand. The women in the group were obviously under-dressed and not corseted, and the men acted rudely—they tried to blend in, but they did a bad job of it. The woman was suspicious because of the attack on Zendaya and called the police helpline. The Grenadiers were already on their way when the attack started.&rdquo;
Anna&rsquo;s eyes widened with interest. &ldquo;That’s fascinating. How did the Freeborn stay uninfected by something as contagious as LASS-VASH-2024? And why form a terrorist group only now, three years after the Change? And where did they get the money for their equipment?&rdquo;
Mara’s fingers paused before she signed, &ldquo;I’ll… use my contacts. We need more information about them. We can’t let this group cause any serious harm.&rdquo;
The women exchanged nods, understanding the seriousness of the situation. Mara’s vague response suggested she had ways of gathering information, and they would discuss it more once she had news.
The conversation then shifted to other topics.
Mara mentioned that she had received the agenda for the upcoming conference on viruses and pandemic control.
Sonia’s fingers moved with curiosity. &ldquo;What’s the focus of the conference?&rdquo;
Mara signed, &ldquo;The conference will cover the medical and legal aspects of pandemic control. It’s a big event for all of us. There will be sessions on developing antiviral treatments, vaccine distribution strategies, and the legal side of pandemic response.&rdquo;
Anna nodded. &ldquo;It sounds like it’ll be really informative. Who’s speaking?&rdquo;
Mara’s hands showed a hint of amusement. &ldquo;One of the keynote speakers is Dr. Cheng, the CEO of CBI.&rdquo; She turned to Anna. &ldquo;And did you know he’s also the CEO of Maylee Shufoo? I found that out for Sonia a long time ago. He’ll be discussing the impact of neuroactive viral diseases and future pandemic preparedness. There are also several other well-known experts from the medical and legal fields.&rdquo;
Sonia&rsquo;s hands froze mid-sign. &ldquo;Dr. Cheng?&rdquo; she signed, her movements quick and anxious. &ldquo;Are you sure?&rdquo;
Mara nodded, noticing Sonia’s reaction. &ldquo;Yes, why? Is something wrong?&rdquo;
Sonia’s hands shook slightly as she signed, &ldquo;When I… met him in Shanghai, three years ago, the… situation wasn’t favorable.&rdquo; From her signs, it was clear there was more to the story. Anna knew the details, but Mara did not, and Sonia wasn’t ready to share. &ldquo;It’s been three years, but I’m worried he might recognize me.&rdquo;
Anna reached over, gently touching Sonia&rsquo;s arm to calm her. &ldquo;Sonia, that was a long time ago. You’re either masked or veiled now, and even if he sees your bare face, he probably wouldn’t recognize you. You’ve changed, and so has the world.&rdquo;
Sonia took a deep breath, trying to steady her hands. &ldquo;I know, but the thought still makes me nervous. He was involved….&rdquo; Her hands paused, then she started again. &ldquo;What if he somehow realizes who I am?&rdquo;
Mara’s eyes softened with understanding. &ldquo;Sonia, you’ve come a long way since then. Dr. Cheng might not even remember you. Besides, we’re going to the conference to learn and make a difference. If you feel uncomfortable, you don’t have to attend his session.&rdquo;
Sonia nodded, her fingers moving more slowly. &ldquo;Thank you, Mara. I appreciate that. I’ll try to focus on the positive aspects of the conference.&rdquo;
Anna signed, &ldquo;It’s normal to feel nervous, but we’re all in this together. We’ll support each other.&rdquo;
Later that week, the conference at the International Conference Center began with a quiet sense of anticipation. The venue, designed to accommodate thousands, had most of its space unused, except for a small section set up for the 200 attendees. The main auditorium had been thoughtfully divided: one half was arranged with locking fempads for unattended women, while the other half was set up for men and their wards. The seating was cleverly designed, allowing the chairs to convert easily from standard seats to secure women&rsquo;s seats with locking arms and modified beds.
Anna, Sonia, and Mara arrived without their guardians. Philippe had programmed Mara’s iGuardian to guide her to the center and had set a geofence to keep her within the conference area. Dressed formally, Mara wore a sleek, dark navy suit with a high-collared blouse that locked at the back. The blouse, made from smooth, matte silk, had delicate lace detailing at the cuffs. Her long skirt fell just above her ballet boots, with a traditional Yoyah Sheengzoh underneath. She also wore matching leather gloves, and a tight bonnet held her mask securely in place, fixed to the collar of her iGuardian.
Sonia chose a more balanced look. She wore a fitted gray pencil skirt with a lavender blouse featuring puffed sleeves and a ruffled collar. Her light gray gloves matched her stylish mask, which had subtle embroidered patterns complementing her outfit. A matching headscarf kept her hair neatly tucked away.
Anna, opting for a more casual style, wore a pale blue dress with a flared skirt and short sleeves that covered her elbow-length gloves. The dress had a playful polka-dot pattern, giving it a relaxed &ldquo;casual Friday&rdquo; vibe. Her mask was simple and plain white, without any embellishments, and she wore a light summer hat pinned to her bun.
The three women made their way to the women’s section and locked themselves into the fempads. They felt the firm grip of the restraints as they settled into place, a reassuring pressure that anchored them in the midst of the growing crowd. The atmosphere was thick with anticipation, though the room was eerily silent, save for the soft clicking of heels and the rustling of fabric as other women took their places. The subdued murmur of male voices drifted from the other side of the room, adding to the quiet tension.
As the lights dimmed, Dr. Cheng stepped onto the stage, ready to deliver his keynote on neuroactive diseases. Sonia, already anxious, felt her heart race as she realized she was now locked into a fempad for a talk given by the very man she had been avoiding. The mask she wore, along with her complete coverage in Changed attire, meant there was little chance of being recognized, yet the anxiety gnawed at her. She had to consciously breathe deeply, forcing herself to stay calm, knowing there was no real danger, though the memories of Shanghai made it hard to relax.
Dr. Cheng began his lecture, titled &ldquo;Neuroactive Parasites and Viruses: Common Pathways from Toxoplasma Gondii to Emerging Human Influences,&rdquo; speaking with the calm authority of someone deeply knowledgeable in his field. Sonia and Anna, both familiar with the LASS-VASH-2024 virus, quickly noticed that Dr. Cheng was only scratching the surface of the virus’s true nature. For them, his presentation was interesting but lacked the depth they knew was possible. However, for most of the audience, his revelations were groundbreaking. He spoke about how a hypothetical virus could influence behavior, and the audience hung on every word.
As the lecture ended, the women were automatically released from their fempads, and they filed out in an orderly manner. The silence was only broken by the sound of their heels and the soft swish of their skirts. The stillness of the event was almost unnerving, with only the occasional murmur of male voices breaking through the quiet.
In the main hall, the space was divided again. The unattended women had their own section, where they could switch from masks to veils modestly for refreshments. Or, in Mara’s case, she had the option to be locked into a women’s chair with a feed bag if she wished to take a break. The wards accompanied by their guardians mingled in the other half, quietly discussing the topics of the day.
Sonia and Mara walked over to the refreshment bar, eyeing the options laid out on the table. Anna, unimpressed by the usual conference fare, stayed back, making a quiet joke about the poor quality of the coffee. Mara picked up a feed bag, reading the label with mild interest.
Suddenly, the kitchen door beside them burst open with a loud crash. A group of armed intruders, their strange breathing masks identifying them as Freeborn, stormed into the room: The door slammed into Mara with brutal force, hitting her body and face. The titanium shell of her iGuardian and her fixed mask absorbed most of the blow and protected her from harm, but the impact still knocked her off her feet. She lost her balance, and fell hard onto her back, her narrow skirt preventing her from getting up. She tried to turn her head to find Sonia, but her locked-on mask held her head rigid. She lay there, trapped and helpless, like an overturned bug unable to right itself.
Around her, muffled cries filled the air—panicked sounds from gagged women who couldn&rsquo;t scream. The clicking of heels echoed as others tried to flee, their movements frantic and chaotic. Then, a gunshot rang out, loud and terrifying, freezing everyone in place. Mara felt a rough hand grab her, flipping her onto her stomach. She felt the cold edge of a knife scrape against the back of her iGuardian, followed by the harsh buzz of a taser.
A powerful shock jolted through her body, sent from her fried iGuardian through all electrodes at once. The pain was overwhelming, blurring her vision as she slipped into unconsciousness.
The intruders worked quickly, rounding up several Changed women, including Sonia and Mara. Within moments, they retreated, leaving behind a scene of chaos and fear. Sonia and Mara, along with the others, were gone, taken by the Freeborn, their fate uncertain.
